WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.575
What makes a run evidence is the
pipeline around the collectors.

2
00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:09.784
The orchestrator runs them in the fixed
order and writes the assessment manifest:

3
00:00:09.784 --> 00:00:15.445
a new GUID for the run; the domain, host
and account; the start, end and duration;

4
00:00:15.445 --> 00:00:21.563
the staleness threshold; and every output
file with its size, time and SHA-256 hash.

5
00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:25.937
A failed step is recorded in the
manifest rather than stopping the run,

6
00:00:25.937 --> 00:00:28.275
so a partial run is visible as partial.

7
00:00:28.275 --> 00:00:31.189
Anyone holding the
repository can recompute the

8
00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:34.175
hashes and show nothing
changed after collection.

9
00:00:34.175 --> 00:00:36.200
Then one run, one commit.

10
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.000
The reference design uses a
self-hosted Gitea instance.

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.279
Each run gets its own branch, named for the
domain and timestamp, and the multi-file

12
00:00:45.279 --> 00:00:50.400
contents endpoint commits the whole run,
manifest included, as a single commit.

13
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.137
The source committed one file per API
call, hundreds of commits per run.

14
00:00:55.137 --> 00:00:59.925
Issues are raised automatically for two
classes only: critical PKI patterns,

15
00:00:59.925 --> 00:01:04.563
and unconstrained delegation on accounts
that aren't domain controllers.

16
00:01:04.563 --> 00:01:09.772
Everything else goes to the planning
documents: GPO reports to the Intune plan,

17
00:01:09.772 --> 00:01:11.696
computers to the device plan,

18
00:01:11.696 --> 00:01:15.944
the PKI report to certificate-based
authentication readiness,

19
00:01:15.944 --> 00:01:21.074
trusts to the partner access plan, and
users and groups to the identity design.

20
00:01:21.074 --> 00:01:24.238
Drift: run weekly and
compare with the last run.

21
00:01:24.238 --> 00:01:26.787
A changed hash tells you
that something changed.

22
00:01:26.787 --> 00:01:30.873
To say what, compare parsed
objects by a stable key,

23
00:01:30.873 --> 00:01:33.862
a GUID or SID, and exclude timestamps.

24
00:01:33.862 --> 00:01:37.899
Schedule under the managed service
account, so no password is stored.

25
00:01:37.899 --> 00:01:41.012
Handling: the data is
a map for an attacker.

26
00:01:41.012 --> 00:01:43.532
Encrypt it, restrict the repository,

27
00:01:43.532 --> 00:01:49.075
keep runs at least twelve months and delete
after thirty-six unless a legal hold

28
00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.754
applies, sign the module,

29
00:01:50.754 --> 00:01:54.701
and keep the API token in a
credential store, never in a URL.

30
00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:58.680
Appendix B lists sixteen corrections
made to the source design.
